In my experience, monsters that can't negotiate water won't
be placed on water.  (They might still be summoned, but
they'll be placed on the nearest dry-land tile.)  If you had
wands of cold and fire you could freeze the water, wait for
things to be generated on the ice, then melt it and drown
them, but that's complicated and prone to not work out
quite as expected when something happens different from
how you anticipate.  Also, it still doesn't handle the various
things that will show up that can negotiate water just fine,
whether by flying (dragons), by not needing to breathe
(vampire lords, master liches), by swimming (krakens
and such) or by just generally being too awesome to for
such mundane things as water to hinder them (the titan
itself).  Also, with a titan about, the wands of fire and
cold would probably run out of charges while there are
still monsters being summoned.

